'' NAMED TUPLE ELEMENTS: 'r.tl.x' for 'r._1._1' -- a tiko extension (fbc's error 18).
'' The names come from the declaration the expression reaches: a 'var' from its
'' initialiser, a call's result, a typedef, a pointer through one, a byref parameter, a
'' UDT field, an array element, a WITH subject. Assignment does not move them, and a
'' positional '_k' always wins over an element NAMED '_k'. See symbols/tuplenames.bas.
''
'' RUN, because a name bound to the wrong element compiles and prints the wrong number.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target win64-msvc tests/driver/src/tuple-names.bas -o tests/driver/tuplenames.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64-msvc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/tuplenames.exe
'' RUN: tests/driver/tuplenames.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: var 100 200 300 400
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: pos 100 200 300 400
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: call 400 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: typedef 5 2 7 8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: other 5 8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ptr 5 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: byref 1 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: field 42 str str
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: array 11 12
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: with 5 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: positional 1 2
